+# Login connection-chip recheck action is keyboard-inoperable (Enter/Space no-op) — WCAG 2.1.1
+
+**Date**: 2026-10-29 20:57+08 (Cycle 39) · **Role**: human-eye · **Route**: `/login` @1440×900 · **Build**: `index-CAV1C5sl.js` (unchanged since 2026-10-27)
+
+## Summary
+
+On `/login`, the live connection-status chip (fed by `GET /api/health-aggregation`, ~20–30s background
+poll) renders an interactive **degraded state: `<button type="button" tabindex="0">` "High Concurrency
+3/5"** whose click action performs an immediate health recheck. The button is reachable by Tab
+(stop 2 from body, visible `outline: solid` focus ring), but **keyboard activation does nothing**:
+neither Enter nor Space fires the recheck. Only pointer/programmatic `click()` works.
+
+- Healthy state: chip "Network Optimal 5/5" (`c37-login-network-optimal-healthy.png`)
+- Degraded state: interactive button "High Concurrency 3/5"
+  (`c37-login-connection-degraded-3of5.png`, `c39-login-chip-focused-keyboard-noop.png`)
+- After keyboard-recovered recheck: `c37-login-recheck-recovered.png`
+
+## Evidence (Playwright/CDP, fresh sessions, 2026-10-29 20:57–21:05+08, degraded payload injected
+via route-mock on `**/api/health-aggregation` — backend itself healthy 5/5)
+
+| # | Action on focused degraded chip | `GET /api/health-aggregation` count | Result |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| T1 | Tab→Tab (activeElement = the chip BUTTON), **Enter** | 2 → **2** (delta 0) | **no recheck** |
+| T1b | repeat, independent session | 6 → **6** (delta 0) | **no recheck** |
+| T2 | same focus, **Space** | 2 → **2** (delta 0) | **no recheck** |
+| T3 | programmatic `chip.click()` (control) | 2 → **4** (delta +2) | recheck fires |
+| T4 | **Enter on "Sign in" button** (global-interception control) | — | **form validation alert fires** ("দয়া করে সব ফিল্ড পূরণ করুন।") |
+
+T4 rules out a page-level Enter interceptor: a native `onClick` button on the same page responds to
+Enter normally. Combined with T1/T1b/T2: the chip's recheck action is wired to **pointer events only**
+(e.g. `onPointerDown`/`onMouseDown` instead of `onClick`), so native button keyboard activation never
+invokes it. `element.click()` dispatches `click` directly and therefore works — matching C37's
+observation that mouse clicks recheck fine.
+
+Element facts (settled read): `tagName=BUTTON`, `type=button`, `tabIndex=0`, `role=null` (native
+semantics), focus outline `solid`, size 195×31.
+
+## Impact
+
+- Keyboard-only users who land on `/login` during a degraded window **see** the chip and can focus it
+  (visible ring), but pressing Enter/Space is silently inert — a WCAG 2.1.1 (Keyboard, Level A)
+  failure for this control and a trap-like dead affordance.
+- Recovery is not fully blocked (background poll ~20–30s self-heals; C37 evidence), so severity is
+  **P2, not P1**: manual recheck is unavailable to keyboard users, automatic recovery still arrives.
+- Screen-reader users get no announcement of the degraded→healthy flip either (chip has no
+  `aria-live`; separate minor note, below WO bar).
+
+## Smallest safe fix
+
+Wire the existing recheck handler to the button's `click` event (or add
+`onKeyDown`: Enter/Space → same handler). One-line-class change in the chip component; no visual
+change, no token changes, no new pattern. Keyboard users get the same immediate-recheck affordance
+pointer users already have.
+
+## Regression test
+
+1. Keyboard: route-mock degraded payload → Tab to chip → Enter → assert a new
+   `GET /api/health-aggregation` fires and the chip updates from the response.
+2. Pointer parity: same setup, `chip.click()` → same assertion (already passing).
+3. a11y sweep: every interactive element on `/login` with `tabIndex >= 0` fires its primary action on
+   Enter **or** Space (guards against pointer-only wiring regressing elsewhere).
+
+## Duplicates / alternatives
+
+- Not covered by #2207 (auth error-feedback UX), #2258/#2298/#2328 (F-12 CORS preflight family),
+  #2205 (health staleness guard) — the chip fetches fine (health-aggregation returns 200 even in the
+  boot burst window); only the **activation path** is broken. No prior WO mentions keyboard operability
+  of this control.
+- Alternative rejected: filing under a generic "audit all buttons for keyboard activation" WO —
+  rejected because Sign in / nav / tabs / model-select all passed keyboard sweeps (C19–C38); this is
+  the first keyboard-inoperable control found in 39 cycles, so a targeted report is proportionate.
+- Alternative rejected: aria-live addition as the fix — orthogonal; announces status but does not make
+  the action operable (2.1.1 still fails).
